# Building & Deploying the Apps

PySide6 desktop apps (Iron661Capture, Parallax Export Studio, OrthoSim) packaged with
**PyInstaller onedir**. Environment: Windows, Python **3.14** (`py -3`). Install deps from
`host/`: `py -3 -m pip install -r requirements.txt -r requirements-build.txt`.
See [HANDOFF.md](mdc:HANDOFF.md) §2–4 and [pkg_issue.md](mdc:docs/pkg_issue.md).

## ⛔ Never build onto Google Drive

The repo lives on `G:\My Drive\…` (a streamed virtual filesystem). If PyInstaller's
`COLLECT` writes the EXE there, the embedded PKG tail is corrupted and the EXE dies at
launch with *"Could not load PyInstaller's embedded PKG archive"*. Smoking gun: COLLECT
takes ~160 s on `G:` vs <30 s on `C:`. **Always redirect `--distpath`/`--workpath` to
local NTFS.** Only the output bytes must be local — the `.spec` can stay on Drive.

```powershell
# ✅ Good: build to local NTFS, then mirror to the deploy folder
$r = Join-Path $env:LOCALAPPDATA 'Iron661Build'
py -3 -m PyInstaller --noconfirm --clean --distpath "$r\dist" --workpath "$r\build" Iron661Capture.spec
.\install_parallax_desktop.ps1   # robocopy /MIR to "C:\Parallax Apps\Iron661 Capture" + desktop shortcut

# ❌ Bad: bare build writes COLLECT onto G:\ → corrupt PKG, dead EXE
py -3 -m PyInstaller Iron661Capture.spec
```

- Run these from `host/`. `install_parallax_desktop.ps1` prefers the local build output
  and mirrors it to `C:\Parallax Apps\…` (note the spaces).
- Do **not** use `build_windows_release.ps1` as-is: `$ErrorActionPreference='Stop'` makes
  it abort when `pip` prints its upgrade notice to stderr. Run the steps above directly.

## Smoke-test the EXE for real

The PKG-corruption popup leaves the process **alive**, so a bare "did it exit?" check
passes on a broken build. Confirm the window actually came up:

```powershell
(Get-Process -Id <pid>).MainWindowTitle   # must be non-empty (e.g. "Iron 661 Capture + Focus (build …)")
```

## Launching a Qt GUI from the agent shell

The agent/automation shell sets `QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen`, so Qt renders invisibly (no
window) even though the process is healthy. Override it when launching for display:

```powershell
$env:QT_QPA_PLATFORM = "windows"
py -3 host/main_capture.py
```

A normal interactive terminal needs no override.

## Git

Commit with `git.exe commit` from `cmd` (the harness appends a `Co-authored-by: … <…>`
trailer whose `<` breaks PowerShell parsing). Stage only intended files — the tree has
pre-existing untracked junk (`Training pictures/`, `RefDesign/`, captures) that must not
be committed. Generated `build/`/`dist/`, logs, and captures are gitignored.
